        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(android): preserve emoji in tool detail previews",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nFixes an issue where Android pending-tool detail previews could show malformed Unicode when a tool argument's first line placed an emoji across the 160-code-unit truncation boundary.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nTool argument previews already truncate at 157 UTF-16 code units before appending an ellipsis. That path now reuses the existing Android `takeUtf16Safe` helper (same helper as session labels / notification text) so a split surrogate pair is dropped instead of rendered. The 160-code-unit size contract is unchanged.\n\n## User Impact\n\nPending tool rows keep valid Unicode when an emoji lands on the detail preview cutoff. Arguments that do not cross the limit render exactly as before.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- Exact head: `3fb22022a493032c686c7a254b8e844c8cc9e494`\n- Added Robolectric coverage for both a split surrogate pair and a complete pair at the 157-code-unit cut via `ToolDisplayRegistry.resolve` for `bash`/`command` (asset-backed `tool-display.json` detailKeys).\n- Current-main negative (UTF-16 code-unit model matching Kotlin `String.length` / `take`): prefix of 156 `a` + `😀` → raw `slice(0, 157)` ends on a high surrogate (`\\ud83d`); `takeUtf16Safe(157)` drops the orphan and yields 156 `a`s. Prefix of 155 `a` + `😀` keeps the full emoji.\n- `git diff --check` clean on the branch.\n- Local Gradle unit test not run here: this environment has no `JAVA_HOME` / `java` on PATH (same contributor-policy skip pattern as recent Android UTF-16 lands). Hosted Android unit CI should execute `ToolDisplayRegistryTest`.\n\nAI-assisted change; no agent transcript attached.\n\nMade with [Cursor](https://cursor.com)",
